From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] rust: bindings and helpers for net_device, NAPI, sk_buff and
 streaming DMA

Adds linux/netdevice.h, etherdevice.h, skbuff.h and if_vlan.h to the Rust
bindings and C helpers for the static inlines (and a few bitfield /
anonymous-union field accessors of struct sk_buff) a NIC driver needs:
netdev_priv, NAPI add/del/schedule/gro_receive, carrier and TX queue state,
BQL, the TX queue lock, eth_hw_addr_set/random, skb head/frag/offload
accessors, netdev_alloc_frag/skb_free_frag/skb_add_rx_frag, and
dma_map_single/unmap_single/mapping_error/sync_single_for_{cpu,device}.
No logic: every helper is a one-line call or field access, so bindgen
checks every signature the driver uses.

Used by the out-of-tree Rust al_eth (ai_re nix/packages/al-eth/rust/knet)
on the opt-in Rust-enabled Alpine kernel only (linux-alpine rustNet = true).

Scope: kernel-rust (7.3.4).
---
diff --color -ruN a/rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h b/rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h
